# Transcrição

Decisão de provider e rationale: `docs/22-transcription-provider-decision.md`.

- Default path is on-device transcription (ONNX/WebGPU with WASM fallback). Audio must not leave the device on this path — no upload, no provider call, nothing but model weights fetched.
- `TranscriptionProvider` is a port with adapters. Never call a provider SDK directly from a component or route; swapping provider must cost an adapter, not a refactor.
- The browser obtains a short-lived `session_capture_grant` from an authenticated endpoint before activating the microphone.
- The same server-side recording/transcription ConsentState gate applies before issuing either the capture grant or any fallback signed-upload capability. Revoked/invalid consent must deny both.
- Because the server does not sit in the audio path locally, enforcement completes at persistence: reject a transcript segment whose capture grant is missing, expired or foreign to the session.
- The optional fallback (Groq) is only available when the organization enables it and `GROQ_API_KEY` is set. That key is server-only and never reaches the browser. With the fallback disabled, the session proceeds without transcription rather than degrading privacy silently.
- Persist final transcript segments incrementally and idempotently; resuming capture must not duplicate text.
- Treat interim transcript as provisional and final transcript as still fallible. Preserve ambiguity/error signals, especially for negation, names, regionalisms and technical terms.
- Diarization is an optional provider capability. When the adapter does not support it, leave segments unlabeled — never synthesize a speaker.
- Do not add emotion recognition from voice/face. Do not allow ASR output alone to become a definitive clinical fact or automatic safety decision.
